Relevant columns & why

• event_date: filter the 31 daily tables that belong to 20201201‑20201231  
• event_params: contains both the flag session_engaged (1 = true) and the session key ga_session_id – both must be extracted with UNNEST()  
• user_pseudo_id: user identifier – will be combined with ga_session_id to form a session key  
• (inside event_params) → key = 'session_engaged', value.int_value: tells whether the session is engaged (=1)  
• (inside event_params) → key = 'ga_session_id', value.int_value: numeric id that, together with user_pseudo_id, defines one session  

Typical conditions

• _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231' – limits to December 2020 tables  
• ep.key = 'session_engaged'   AND   ep.value.int_value = 1 – keeps only engaged sessions  
• gs.key = 'ga_session_id' – picks the session id  
• DISTINCT user_pseudo_id, ga_session_id – removes duplicate event rows that belong to the same session  

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Below are ten exploratory → increasingly complete SQL statements (each returns ≤20 rows) that show the necessary steps and end with the final query that produces the average engaged‑sessions‑per‑user figure.

```sql
-- 1. Peek at one December table to see some event_params keys
SELECT
  `event_name`,
  ep.key,
  ep.value.int_value,
  ep.value.string_value
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201201`,
     UNNEST(`event_params`) AS ep
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Check how the 'session_engaged' flag looks on a single day
SELECT
  `user_pseudo_id`,
  ep.value.int_value AS session_engaged
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201205`,
     UNNEST(`event_params`) AS ep
WHERE ep.key = 'session_engaged'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Retrieve ga_session_id together with the engaged flag for one table
SELECT
  `user_pseudo_id`,
  MAX(CASE WHEN ep.key = 'ga_session_id'     THEN ep.value.int_value END) AS ga_session_id,
  MAX(CASE WHEN ep.key = 'session_engaged'   THEN ep.value.int_value END) AS session_engaged
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201207`,
     UNNEST(`event_params`) AS ep
GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. List distinct engaged sessions for 1 day (engaged = 1)
SELECT DISTINCT
  `user_pseudo_id`,
  gs.value.int_value AS ga_session_id
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201209`,
     UNNEST(`event_params`) AS se,          -- session_engaged
     UNNEST(`event_params`) AS gs           -- ga_session_id
WHERE se.key = 'session_engaged'
  AND se.value.int_value = 1
  AND gs.key = 'ga_session_id'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Same as #4 but using WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX to handle multiple days with a wildcard
SELECT DISTINCT
  `user_pseudo_id`,
  gs.value.int_value AS ga_session_id,
  _TABLE_SUFFIX AS event_table
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*`,
     UNNEST(`event_params`) AS se,
     UNNEST(`event_params`) AS gs
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'
  AND se.key = 'session_engaged'
  AND se.value.int_value = 1
  AND gs.key = 'ga_session_id'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Count engaged sessions per user for the whole month
SELECT
  `user_pseudo_id`,
  COUNT(DISTINCT CONCAT(CAST(gs.value.int_value AS STRING))) AS engaged_sessions
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*`,
     UNNEST(`event_params`) AS se,
     UNNEST(`event_params`) AS gs
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'
  AND se.key = 'session_engaged'
  AND se.value.int_value = 1
  AND gs.key = 'ga_session_id'
GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Show distribution: users having ≥2 engaged sessions
SELECT
  engaged_sessions,
  COUNT(*) AS users
FROM (
  SELECT
    `user_pseudo_id`,
    COUNT(DISTINCT gs.value.int_value) AS engaged_sessions
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*`,
       UNNEST(`event_params`) AS se,
       UNNEST(`event_params`) AS gs
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'
    AND se.key = 'session_engaged'
    AND se.value.int_value = 1
    AND gs.key = 'ga_session_id'
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
)
GROUP BY engaged_sessions
ORDER BY engaged_sessions
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Raw totals needed for the average (will return only one row)
SELECT
  COUNT(DISTINCT user_pseudo_id)                                 AS total_users,
  COUNT(DISTINCT CONCAT(user_pseudo_id,'-',gs.value.int_value))  AS total_engaged_sessions
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*`,
     UNNEST(`event_params`) AS se,
     UNNEST(`event_params`) AS gs
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'
  AND se.key = 'session_engaged'
  AND se.value.int_value = 1
  AND gs.key = 'ga_session_id'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Average engaged sessions per user (simple division)
SELECT
  SAFE_DIVIDE(
    COUNT(DISTINCT CONCAT(user_pseudo_id,'-',gs.value.int_value)),
    COUNT(DISTINCT user_pseudo_id)
  ) AS avg_engaged_sessions_per_user
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*`,
     UNNEST(`event_params`) AS se,
     UNNEST(`event_params`) AS gs
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'
  AND se.key = 'session_engaged'
  AND se.value.int_value = 1
  AND gs.key = 'ga_session_id'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL query – returns only the requested metric (no LIMIT needed)
SELECT
  SAFE_DIVIDE(
    COUNT(DISTINCT CONCAT(user_pseudo_id,'-',gs.value.int_value)),
    COUNT(DISTINCT user_pseudo_id)
  ) AS avg_engaged_sessions_per_user_dec_2020
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*`,
     UNNEST(`event_params`) AS se,
     UNNEST(`event_params`) AS gs
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'          -- December 2020
  AND se.key = 'session_engaged'
  AND se.value.int_value = 1                                   -- engaged = 1
  AND gs.key = 'ga_session_id';
```

